@* The browser tab's title, in one shape: "Games — Spirit Island Companion".

   Every page said this for itself, and the two halves of the app had drifted — the public
   reference pages carried the site name and their signed-in twins did not, so the same
   catalogue read as "Spirits — Spirit Island Companion" on one route and a bare "Spirits" on
   the other. With a dozen tabs open the bare ones name nothing.

   The landing page is the exception and sets <PageTitle> directly: it is the site, so
   "Spirit Island Companion — Spirit Island Companion" is not the name it wants. *@

<PageTitle>@Title — @SiteName</PageTitle>

@code {
    /// <summary>What this page is, in a word or two — "Games", "New game", the match's name.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = "";

    public const string SiteName = "Spirit Island Companion";
}
